---
/* Group therapy is the single most-dreaded part of treatment and one of the
   highest-intent informational searches around it ("do you have to talk in
   group therapy"). This section exists to answer that honestly rather than
   reassure vaguely. */
const truths = [
  { h: 'You do not have to speak on day one', p: 'Sitting there saying nothing is a completely normal first group, and nobody in the room will find it remarkable. Most people listen for a few sessions before they say anything real.' },
  { h: 'Everyone there arrived dreading it too', p: 'The room is not full of people who find this easy. It is full of people who were where you are within the last few weeks, which is precisely why it works better than talking to someone who was not.' },
  { h: 'It is not a confession', p: 'Nobody is required to produce their worst story on demand. Groups are structured around what is happening now and what to do about it, rather than around performing your history.' },
  { h: 'Twice a day sounds like a lot', p: 'It does, and for the first few days it feels like it. Then it becomes the thing that gives the day a shape, and most people find they would rather be in the room than in their own head.' },
];
---
<section id="group-fear" class="bg-sage-tint py-[70px]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
          The bit everyone dreads
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-6">"Do I have to talk in group?"</h2>
        <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-charcoal text-[17px] leading-[29px]">
          <p>
            It is the most common thing people are quietly worried about, and it puts more people off treatment than the detox does. So, plainly: no, not straight away, and not before you are ready.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">What tends to happen is more ordinary than the fear.</strong> You sit in a room. Somebody describes something you recognise. At some point you say so out loud, and it turns out to be a great deal less frightening than a month of rehearsing it in your head.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <a href="tel:8883625576" class="bg-teal hover:bg-teal-dark text-white font-bold px-7 py-3.5 rounded-lg transition-colors font-body tracking-wide inline-block">
            Ask us what it is like
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {truths.map(t => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-7 border border-cream-soft">
            <h3 class="font-display text-[20px] leading-[26px] text-navy mb-3">{t.h}</h3>
            <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[26px]">{t.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
